Sval: read a globally defaulted permission denial as "prompt"

A new RFPTarget, PermissionsDefaultDenyPrompt, makes navigator.permissions
.query report "prompt", and Notification.permission "default", where the deny
comes only from a global default (permissions.default.<type>, such as
blocking every notification request) and the deciding principal has no
permission entry of its own.

PermissionDelegateHandler::GetPermission already decides which principal a
document's permission comes from, so it also reports whether that answer is
a default deny (PermissionDelegateHandler::IsDefaultDeny: no entry from
PermissionManager::GetPermissionObject, deny from TestPermissionFromPrincipal).
A frame whose top document is in another process reads the top's delegated
list, which carries the same bit, computed where the top's principal is.
GetPermissionForPermissionsAPI hides only that case. A site the user
blocked, a deny from feature policy, and ePersistDeniedCrossOrigin's deny,
which every user's cross-origin frame gets, all stay "denied". A worker with
no window decides with its own principal and hides the same way.
Notification.permission (GetNotificationPermission, for the attribute only)
applies the same rule, so the two agree.

No chrome API can change what these report.

